---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Megan"
  description="Meet Megan Feng, an Omaha student photographer, cellist, writer, and school-community leader."
  image="/images/work/photo-40-1600.webp"
>
  <section class="quiet-about-hero">
    <div class="about-introduction" data-reveal>
      <p class="micro-label">Behind the camera</p>
      <h1>Hi, I’m<br>Megan Feng.</h1>
      <p>
        I’m a sophomore at Millard North High School in Omaha. I make photographs because I want to remember what it felt like to be there—not only what it looked like.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="about-portrait" data-reveal>
      <img src="/images/work/photo-40-1600.webp" alt="Playful studio portrait with a heart made around one eye" width="2048" height="1477">
      <figcaption>The other side of the lens</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="about-detail" data-reveal>
      <img src="/images/work/photo-42-800.webp" alt="Camera equipment arranged on a white surface" width="800" height="533">
      <figcaption>What comes along</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="about-statement">
    <p class="micro-label" data-reveal>How I see</p>
    <blockquote data-reveal>
      I’m drawn to people who are completely in the moment—competing, creating, laughing, and being themselves.
    </blockquote>
    <div class="about-columns" data-reveal>
      <p>
        Sports taught me to anticipate. Orchestra taught me to listen. Debate taught me to look at the same thing from more than one angle. Those habits follow me every time I pick up a camera.
      </p>
      <p>
        At school, I photograph Swim & Dive, create social content, play principal cello in Philharmonic Orchestra, and participate in Debate and Student Council. Away from school, I assist young string students and volunteer with children through the Munroe-Meyer Institute.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-record">
    <header data-reveal>
      <p class="micro-label">Recent notes</p>
      <h2>Outside the frame</h2>
    </header>
    <ol>
      <li data-reveal>
        <span>2026</span>
        <div><h3>Writing</h3><p>Scholastic Art & Writing Awards Silver Key in personal essay and Honorable Mention in poetry; both pieces published.</p></div>
      </li>
      <li data-reveal>
        <span>2026</span>
        <div><h3>Music</h3><p>Division I string quintet and Division II cello solo at NSAA District Music Contest; Highly Superior at the ASTA Young Orchestra Festival.</p></div>
      </li>
      <li data-reveal>
        <span>2026</span>
        <div><h3>School community</h3><p>Ran Mustang Mart, created Orchestra senior slideshow and posts, and was nominated for the MPS Diversity Retreat.</p></div>
      </li>
      <li data-reveal>
        <span>2025—now</span>
        <div><h3>Showing up</h3><p>Assistant string teacher, volunteer, orchestra leader, team manager, social media coordinator, and debater.</p></div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="about-closing" data-reveal>
    <img src="/images/work/photo-29-1600.webp" alt="A student lying in bright grass and looking toward the camera" width="2048" height="1438" loading="lazy">
    <div>
      <p class="micro-label">Keep looking</p>
      <h2>The photographs<br>say the rest.</h2>
      <a href="/#work">Return to portfolio →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
